## Per Template

For each template ensure:

1. The theme is retoken compatible (https://kieranwood.ca/retoken/theme/)
2. It includes the following components on top of the normal form fields, buttons, typography, images, `<dialog>` modals, etc.
  1. Accordion (just use `<details><summary></summary></details>`, but also give options for combining a bunch of them together into a larger group)
  2. Cards
    1. Typical setup
      1. Heading
      2. description
      3. icon or image
    2. include horizontal variants with images/icons on the left or right side
    3. include 1 more dynamic card with some sort of an effect that makes sense for the tempalte
  3. fifty-fifty
    1. Image takes up 50% of the component size, text takes up the rest
    2. e.g https://web.ucalgary.ca/blocks-layouts/block-library-guide/image-text-block
    3. image on left or right
  4. Image gallery with lightbox
  5. toggle switch (for themes where plain checkboxes make less sense)
  6. page break (a `<hr>`)
  7. Any flare elements you find that are necessary for putting together demo pages
3. Prefer semantic html over `div`'s (e.g. `<details>` for accordions, `<dialogue>` for modals, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`, etc.)
4. Do not use any frameworks, all pure HTML, and CSS with no build step, **minimal** js, only used when absolutely required
5. Each should have a sidebar and normal navbar variant
6. All templates need a light and dark theme
7. For docs there should be a library of all components for people to see, similar to https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components
8. File structure should be that it lives in `tempaltes/<tempalte-name>` with the following directories and files
  1. `index.html` an overview page to show off the theme, give it normal prose and tie the elements together nicely, with links to the other pages somewhere
  2. `blogpost.html` an example blogpost with all markdown standard featuers (tables, images, italics, headings, etc.), and things like an author card with metadata like tags, date published, etc.
  3. `forms.html` an example form
  4. `sidebar.html` a sidebar variant
  5. `docs/` a folder containing docs-style pages for the template
    1. `docs/component/<component-name>.html` a page for each component to show it off with docs about the component and a copy-paste option to be able to use it
    2. `docs/defaults.html` Page for generic HTML elements; elements like `<h2>`
    3. A page to show off a blog post design
    4. A page with a quick get-started section
  6. `example` an example website with 3 pages, 1 homepage and 2 others that make sense, to get a feel for it in a "real" project
9. Include it in the lading page

## Per change
Required guidence to follow per change

- Check off changes as you go
  - Make sure the TODO is kept up to date so that if a usage limit is hit I'm not left in the dark
- Add Changes to the CHANGELOG.md
    - If a version exists and does not have a release date yet, keep adding to it, if there's no versions without a release date, then bump version (e.g. `v0.1.0 -> v0.2.0`) in the version file, and add a new main heading to CHANGELOG.md for it (e.g. `v0.2.0 (unreleased)`) and add the changes under there.
    - Be brief, 2-4 setnences per change, and if you need more, prompt for approval from the user
    - Add all changes under the following categories as sub-headings:
      - Features
      - Bug Fixes
      - Other
        - For things like
          - Documentation improvements
          - Refinements to existing systems that weren't bugs
          - anything else that doesn't fit in the other sections